# Voice Modes - Dictation vs Agent ✅

## Two Distinct Voice Interaction Modes

Juno implements **two completely separate voice interaction modes** that share the same voice transcription infrastructure but serve entirely different purposes and workflows.

## Dictation Mode

### Purpose
**Immediate voice-to-text typing** - replaces keyboard input for fast text entry.

### Activation
- **Trigger**: Configurable key (default: spacebar)
- **Behavior**: Hold key down to record, release to commit
- **UI State**: Orange microphone icon

### Workflow
```
Voice Input → Transcription → Text Insertion at Cursor Location
```

### Characteristics
- **No AI Processing**: Pure voice transcription service
- **Immediate Output**: Text appears at current cursor position
- **No Intelligence**: Direct speech-to-text conversion only
- **Use Case**: Replaces typing for emails, documents, code comments, etc.
- **Similar To**: Built-in macOS dictation feature

### Technical Implementation
- **Backend**: [src-tauri/src/spacebar_monitor.rs](mdc:src-tauri/src/spacebar_monitor.rs)
- **Events**: `dictation-transcription-start`, `dictation-transcription-finish`
- **State**: `dictation_active` flag prevents AI processing
- **Timing**: 0ms start, 500ms commitment threshold

## Agent Mode

### Purpose
**AI agent conversations and task execution** - full Computer Use capabilities.

### Activation
- **Trigger**: Alt+D (Option+D on macOS)
- **Behavior**: Toggle to start/stop agent interaction
- **UI State**: Blue microphone icon, full chat interface

### Workflow
```
Voice Input → Transcription → AI Agent Processing → Agent Response/Actions
```

### Characteristics
- **Full AI Processing**: Hierarchical agent system with orchestrator and specialists
- **Computer Use Tools**: All 17 Anthropic actions (screenshot, mouse, keyboard, etc.)
- **Task Execution**: Can perform complex multi-step computer automation
- **Conversational**: Maintains conversation history and context
- **Use Case**: AI assistant for computer automation, coding, research, etc.

### Technical Implementation
- **Backend**: [src-tauri/src/anthropic.rs](mdc:src-tauri/src/anthropic.rs) - Orchestrator agent
- **Events**: `app-dictation-started`, `app-dictation-finished`
- **Architecture**: Multi-agent system with browser, desktop, file specialists
- **Memory**: Persistent conversation history

## Key Distinctions

### Completely Separate Workflows
| Aspect | Dictation Mode | Agent Mode |
|--------|----------------|------------|
| **Purpose** | Voice typing replacement | AI conversation & automation |
| **Output** | Text at cursor | AI responses/actions |
| **Processing** | Transcription only | Full AI agent system |
| **UI** | Orange mic | Blue mic + chat interface |
| **Memory** | None | Persistent conversation |
| **Tools** | None | All Computer Use tools |

### Shared Infrastructure
- **Voice Transcription**: Both use the same Whisper.cpp-based transcription engine
- **Audio Capture**: Same microphone input and processing pipeline
- **Plugin System**: Both leverage [tauri-plugin-voice-transcription](mdc:tauri-plugin-voice-transcription)
- **Event System**: Common transcription events, different result handling

### State Management
```rust
// Backend coordination prevents conflicts
let is_dictation_active = app_state.dictation_active.lock()
    .map(|active| *active)
    .unwrap_or(false);

if is_dictation_active {
    // Route to immediate typing (Dictation Mode)
    return;
}
// Route to AI agent (Agent Mode)
```

## Implementation Guidelines

### Terminology Standards
- **NEVER** use "spacebar mode" - always "Dictation Mode"
- **NEVER** use "option D mode" - always "Agent Mode"
- **ALWAYS** specify which mode when discussing voice features
- **REMEMBER**: Keyboard shortcuts are configurable, modes are functional

### UI State Management
```typescript
// Frontend state differentiation
const [isDictationMode, setIsDictationMode] = useState(false);
const [barState, setBarState] = useState<BarState>("default");

// State mappings:
// "dictating" - Orange microphone (Dictation Mode)
// "listening" - Blue microphone (Agent Mode)
```

### Event Handling
```typescript
// Dictation Mode events
unlistenDictationStart = await listen("dictation-transcription-start", () => {
    setIsDictationMode(true);
    setBarState("dictating");
});

// Agent Mode events
unlistenAgentStart = await listen("app-dictation-started", () => {
    setIsDictationMode(false);
    setBarState("listening");
});
```

## User Documentation Pattern

When documenting voice features:

✅ **CORRECT**:
- "Dictation Mode (default spacebar) for voice typing"
- "Agent Mode (Alt+D) for AI conversations"

❌ **INCORRECT**:
- "Spacebar mode"
- "Option D toggle"

This ensures documentation remains accurate even if keyboard shortcuts change in the future.
